                  <story-point caption='Key Insight: The analysis reveals that operational bottlenecks and errors are heavily concentrated in specific categories and locations—specifically, Sandy experiences a disproportionate volume of &quot;Double Booked&quot; errors in high-demand gear like backpacks and skis, while damages peak during spring inventory turnover months.' captured-sheet='Where Are the Errors?' id='1' />
                  <story-point caption='Addressing the Consulting Question: This highlights that WOC&apos;s digital infrastructure failures are not uniform; they stem from localized inventory scheduling flaws rather than system-wide capacity limits.' captured-sheet='Where Are the Errors?' id='2' />
                  <story-point caption='Supporting Recommendations: In the final presentation, these insights will justify recommending an automated inventory locking system and localized buffer stock rules at high-error branches (like Sandy and Park City) to eliminate double-booking overlaps.' captured-sheet='Where Are the Errors?' id='3' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{B4828EEA-E38A-4403-A38B-C6396289C443}' />
    </dashboard>
